WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.456 --> 00:00:16.602
That afternoon Aunt Polly and Pollyanna went shopping for clothes.

2
00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:23.144
After visiting five stores, Aunt Polly was exhausted.

3
00:00:26.406 --> 00:00:31.648
The clerks were amused by Pollyanna's conversation, and Pollyanna was delighted with the whole excursion.

4
00:00:33.248 --> 00:00:37.011
Waiting for the last package to be wrapped, Pollyanna beamed with happiness.

5
00:00:37.031 --> 00:00:43.056
"My clothes have always come from a church donation box," she explained to the clerk.

6
00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:49.042
"You can't imagine how lovely it is to have beautiful new clothes that fit!"

7
00:00:52.965 --> 00:00:57.068
After supper Aunt Polly recovered from the shopping excursion by visiting a neighbor.

8
00:00:58.189 --> 00:01:01.072
Pollyanna sat in the backyard, chatting with Tom and Nancy.

9
00:01:02.984 --> 00:01:08.346
Tom told Pollyanna many wonderful things about her mother, while Nancy described the farm where her own family

10
00:01:08.386 --> 00:01:14.629
lived. "If Miss Polly lets me, I'll take you there sometime," Nancy promised Pollyanna.

11
00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:17.650
"But now it's time for you to go to bed."

12
00:01:20.792 --> 00:01:23.353
Pollyanna lit a candle and climbed the steps to the attic.

13
00:01:26.654 --> 00:01:28.455
Her little room was as hot as an oven.

14
00:01:30.764 --> 00:01:32.906
With a sigh, she looked at the two closed windows.

15
00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:41.471
"I wish I could open them," she said, "but Aunt Polly said I must wait until the screens

16
00:01:41.532 --> 00:01:48.156
come." After neatly folding her clothes, Pollyanna blew out the candle and got into bed.

17
00:01:49.337 --> 00:01:52.459
Unable to sleep, she tossed and turned for what seemed like hours.

18
00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:59.224
Finally, she slipped out of bed and felt her way through the darkness to her door.

19
00:02:01.696 --> 00:02:05.677
"Maybe there's a window with screens in the main part of the attic," she said.

20
00:02:08.398 --> 00:02:12.239
Pollyanna followed a beam of moonlight through the dark attic to a window.

21
00:02:12.259 --> 00:02:17.080
"Oh dear, there's no screen here either.

22
00:02:18.981 --> 00:02:20.901
But wait a minute, what's that?"

23
00:02:22.262 --> 00:02:25.883
Just below the window, Pollyanna spotted a wide, flat roof.

24
00:02:25.903 --> 00:02:29.964
"If only I could sleep out there!"

25
00:02:31.796 --> 00:02:34.757
Behind her were the vast dark attic and her hot room.

26
00:02:36.457 --> 00:02:40.239
Ahead of her—through the window—were the moonlight and the cool night air.

27
00:02:43.119 --> 00:02:47.281
Suddenly Pollyanna noticed a row of long white bags hanging from nails.

28
00:02:47.301 --> 00:02:52.702
"Nancy said those bags contain winter clothing, put away for the summer."

29
00:02:53.963 --> 00:02:55.583
Pollyanna studied the garment bags.

30
00:02:55.603 --> 00:02:58.244
"Maybe I could turn them into a bed."

31
00:02:59.872 --> 00:03:03.055
Pollyanna selected a soft, thick bag for a mattress.

32
00:03:04.336 --> 00:03:06.218
She could fold up a thinner bag for a pillow.

33
00:03:07.779 --> 00:03:11.262
Gleefully, Pollyanna gathered up the bags and dropped them out the window.

34
00:03:13.764 --> 00:03:16.887
Then she carefully climbed outside, closing the window behind her.

35
00:03:18.848 --> 00:03:22.491
Taking deep breaths of the refreshing air, Pollyanna danced with delight.

36
00:03:24.073 --> 00:03:27.596
She walked from one end of the roof to the other with no fear of falling off.

37
00:03:31.724 --> 00:03:35.748
Finally, with a sigh of contentment, she arranged the garment bags into a bed.

38
00:03:37.229 --> 00:03:39.851
Settling down, she gazed at the star-filled sky.

39
00:03:39.871 --> 00:03:51.902
"I'm glad the screens haven't come yet," she said sleepily, "because now I can enjoy this lovely outdoor

40
00:03:51.962 --> 00:03:58.828
bed." Meanwhile, downstairs in her room, Aunt Polly heard noises on the roof.

41
00:04:01.352 --> 00:04:04.233
She hurried into her bathrobe and slippers, and then phoned Tom.

42
00:04:04.253 --> 00:04:05.953
"Come quick!

43
00:04:06.293 --> 00:04:07.754
Bring a lantern and a ladder!"

44
00:04:08.174 --> 00:04:09.774
Aunt Polly instructed Tom.

45
00:04:09.794 --> 00:04:11.735
"Somebody's on the roof.

46
00:04:12.295 --> 00:04:15.076
I'm going upstairs to make sure the attic window is locked."

47
00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:23.038
A few minutes later, Pollyanna was startled awake by Tom shining a lantern in her face.

48
00:04:24.979 --> 00:04:28.980
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly cried in astonishment from the attic window.

49
00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.300
"What are you doing out there?"

50
00:04:33.061 --> 00:04:34.481
Pollyanna blinked and sat up.

51
00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:39.823
"I was so hot inside, but don't worry, Aunt Polly.

52
00:04:40.903 --> 00:04:45.004
I shut the window after I came out, so flies couldn't carry germs inside."

53
00:04:46.865 --> 00:04:49.265
Tom smiled and quickly disappeared down the ladder.

54
00:04:49.285 --> 00:04:55.527
"Hand those garment bags to me at once and come inside," Aunt Polly said to her niece.

55
00:04:57.368 --> 00:05:00.678
To herself she muttered, "Such an unusual child!"

56
00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.744
After being outdoors, Pollyanna thought the attic air felt even more stifling.

57
00:05:08.745 --> 00:05:09.866
But she didn't complain.

58
00:05:12.408 --> 00:05:17.312
Outside Pollyanna's room Aunt Polly said, "For the rest of the night, you'll sleep in my room.

59
00:05:17.672 --> 00:05:22.396
The screens will arrive tomorrow, but until then it's my duty to know where you are."

60
00:05:24.438 --> 00:05:26.420
Pollyanna's eyes widened in delight.

61
00:05:27.676 --> 00:05:29.879
"How perfectly lovely!

62
00:05:29.899 --> 00:05:34.544
I've always wanted to share a room with someone who belongs to me!"

63
00:05:34.565 --> 00:05:40.892
On the way to her room, Aunt Polly felt both bewildered and helpless.

64
00:05:43.715 --> 00:05:47.260
Once again, Pollyanna had turned a punishment into a reward.
